yaml/key
description: Any scalar before the colon - a string, an integer, or the null key
- >
  A key is ANY scalar, in any style - most often plain, quoted when it needs punctuation. An
  integer-shaped plain scalar is an INTEGER key, and the null scalar makes the NULL key - see
  its subchapter below. (YAML also allows a whole structure as a key via the explicit `? `
  form - rarely seen in practice.)
- !!<format: text/x-yaml> |
  age: 1
  'first name': 2
  "tab\there": 3
  42: 4
  ~: 5
- *..:..:..:..:01-yaml_scalar
- *: 00-yaml_key_null
